🌍 Global Impact
EcoFuelZ is designed to address three critical global challenges simultaneously: Energy Poverty, Climate Change, and Water Scarcity.

1. Closing the Carbon Loop
Unlike traditional fossil fuels, EcoFuelZ creates a Circular Carbon Economy. It captures carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and converts it into usable fuel. When this fuel is burned, it releases only the CO₂ that was originally captured, resulting in a net-zero carbon footprint. This transforms carbon from a pollutant into a renewable resource.

2. Reducing Deforestation & Indoor Pollution
In many developing regions, households rely on wood, charcoal, or dung for cooking. This leads to:

Deforestation: Depletion of local forests for firewood.
Health Issues: Indoor air pollution from solid fuels causes millions of premature deaths annually, disproportionately affecting women and children.
EcoFuelZ provides clean-burning methane, eliminating smoke and reducing the reliance on forest resources.

3. Water Security
By generating clean water as a byproduct of the fuel synthesis process, the system provides a secondary lifeline in water-stressed regions. This is crucial for communities facing drought or contaminated groundwater.

4. Energy Independence & Resilience
Centralized energy grids are vulnerable to disruption from natural disasters, conflicts, or infrastructure failure. EcoFuelZ is fully decentralized. It empowers individuals and communities to generate their own fuel and water, fostering true energy sovereignty.

📍 Where It Can Be Used
This system is designed for Decentralized Resilience. It is most effective in scenarios where:

Remote & Off-Grid Villages: Communities without access to natural gas pipelines or reliable electricity grids.
Disaster Relief Zones: Providing essential cooking fuel and purified water on-site when supply chains are broken.
Urban Slums: Offering a sustainable alternative to intermittent or unaffordable energy sources.
Military & Frontier Outposts: Remote bases requiring fuel and water independence.
Eco-Conscious Living: Households seeking to reduce their carbon footprint and achieve self-sufficiency.
⚡ Features
Input: Sunlight, Air, Water.
Output: Methane (Cooking Gas) + Clean Water.
Efficiency: ~65-70% (Round-trip) via Zero-Cost Engineering Hacks.
Safety: Integrated H₂ leak detection and pressure relief logic.
Accessibility: Designed to be built with locally sourced, non-proprietary components.
🚀 Quick Start (Assembly)
Fabricate Reactor: Roll SS304 pipe, install end caps with 1/4" NPT ports.
Build Electrolyzer: Cut 7x SS plates. Assemble in acrylic sandwich with gaskets.
Mounting: Strap the Electrolyzer stack directly to the Reactor body using hose clamps. (Critical for thermal efficiency).
Electronics: Upload src/firmware.ino to Arduino. Wire Relay module to Electrolyzer positive line.
Plumbing: Connect Water Jug -> Pump -> Electrolyzer -> Reactor -> Condenser Coil -> Gas Bag.
