SAFETY PROTOCOL ⚠️
READ THIS BEFORE ASSEMBLY

This device generates explosive gases (Hydrogen and Methane).

1. Ventilation
NEVER operate indoors or in confined spaces.
H2 accumulates at the ceiling.
CH4 accumulates at the ceiling.
Operate in an open balcony, garden, or well-ventilated shed.

2. Leak Detection
The MQ-8 sensor is MANDATORY.
Test your MQ-8 sensor with a small lighter flame leak before trusting it.
If the alarm triggers, cut power immediately and evacuate the area until gas dissipates.

3. Pressure Safety
Do not seal the reactor completely. Always have a Pressure Relief Valve (PRV) rated for 15-20 bar.
Never block the gas output line while the reactor is heating.

4. Chemical Safety
KOH (Potassium Hydroxide) is caustic. It burns skin.
Always wear gloves and eye protection when handling electrolyte.
If KOH touches skin, wash with plenty of water and vinegar (weak acid).

6. docs/ASSEMBLY_GUIDE.md
Assembly Guide - EcoFuelZ v7.1

Step 1: The Reactor Vessel
Take a stainless steel pipe (SS304, 1 inch OD, 25cm length).
Weld or screw on end caps with 1/4" NPT ports.
Fill the pipe with a mix of Nickel catalyst pellets and Zeolite 4A (Water sorbent).
Wrap the reactor body with Ceramic Wool insulation.
Wrap Silicone Heating Tape over the insulation.
Mount the Electrolyzer: Use hose clamps to strap the acrylic electrolyzer stack directly onto the hot reactor body. This is critical for thermal efficiency.

Step 2: The Electrolyzer (Dry Cell)

Cut 7 stainless steel plates (10x10cm).
Drill a small hole (5mm) at the bottom of each plate for fluid flow.
Assemble the stack: Plate -> Rubber Gasket -> Plate -> Rubber Gasket. Repeat.
Compress the stack between two acrylic sheets using long bolts.
Connect the positive and negative wires to the outer plates (Bipolar configuration).

Step 3: The DAC Column
Pack a PVC pipe with Zeolite 13X pellets.
Mount a 12V DC fan at the inlet to push air through the pellets.
Connect the outlet of the column to the Reactor input port.

Step 4: Plumbing & Heat Exchange
Connect the Electrolyzer output (H₂) to the Reactor.
Connect the Reactor gas output to a Copper Coil.
Critical Step: Place the Copper Coil inside the Water Jug (Electrolyte reservoir). This pre-heats the water and cools the gas.
Connect the Copper Coil output to the Gas Storage Bag via a Flame Arrestor.

Step 5: Electronics
Upload firmware.ino to Arduino.
Connect Relay Module to the Electrolyzer power line.
Connect Thermistor to the Reactor body.
Connect MQ-8 Sensor near the Electrolyzer.


